# question: Can coinciding alarms be identified whom together form a different clinical meaning than their independent meaning, and for which no individual alarm exists?
# rationale: Two independently-derived mda:ClinicalEvent tags (one per
#   PhysiologicalProcess, entailed by clinicalEvents.ttl's single-alarm
#   axioms) coincide in the same tick's situational graph, and their
#   SPECIFIC combination is looked up against a fixed table of recognised
#   syndromes. The table entry supplies the emergent concept
#   (clinicalEvent:CardioRespiratoryArrest) -- it is the query that asserts
#   the combination means something, not the reasoner: OWL-RL cannot
#   conditionally mint a new value from two otherwise-unconnected
#   individuals (see clinicalEvents.ttl's header for why), so this is
#   exactly as far as a declarative axiom can go, and a procedural SPARQL
#   SELECT is required for the rest -- the same division of labour CAT3a's
#   own rule (CODE/evaluation_poc/reasoner/rules/
#   cat3a_cardiorespiratory_arrest.rq) already uses for the operational
#   engine. This query is the tick-snapshot-style answer to the same
#   question CAT3a answers arrival-ordered.
#
# SUPERSEDES the diagnostic version of this query (see ../cq_discoveries.md's
# CQ11 entry for the original finding: "the framework has no vocabulary or
# inference mechanism for an emergent, combined-alarm concept, so no query
# can actually answer this CQ"). That gap is closed: FRAMEWORK/KNOWLEDGE_BASE/
# clinicalEvents.ttl now provides mda:impliesClinicalEvent (PhysiologicalProcess-
# scoped -- see that file's "RECONSIDERED AGAIN" note on why it moved off
# Metric -- mda:situational-tagged, so it reaches this snapshot the same way
# hasRate/hasQualityState already did) plus the two single-alarm axioms
# (CardiacArrestCondition, RespiratoryArrestCondition) that put a
# clinicalEvent: tag on the Process reached from a Metric whose own hasRate
# is Absent. This query is the true answer: it reports every patient/tick
# where two DISTINCT Process individuals each carry a recognised half of a
# known combination, naming the combined meaning -- not just flagging that
# unrelated processes coincide, the way the diagnostic version did.
#
# Deliberately ONE direction, not symmetric like cat3a_cardiorespiratory_
# arrest.rq's FILTER: that rule's symmetry exists because it is evaluated
# PER ARRIVING ALARM, and either half may be the one arriving second. This
# query has no "arriving" alarm at all -- it inspects an already-complete
# tick snapshot -- so binding ?cardiacProcess/?respiratoryProcess to fixed,
# distinct roles finds every genuine coincidence exactly once, with no
# mirror-image duplicate row to filter back out.
#
# Extending to a second combination (e.g. a future VentilationFailure
# axiom pairing a therapeutic-modality fact with a pulmonary-function
# Metric) means adding a second WHERE block/BIND pair here, not rewriting
# this one -- the shape is a lookup, not a general-purpose N-way combiner,
# because clinicalEvents.ttl only ever defines syndromes pairwise and by
# name; a generic "any two distinct impliesClinicalEvent values coincide"
# version would over-report (every combination would look equally
# meaningful, when only specific pairs actually are).
#
# reasoning: required (same graph-shape notes as CQ9/CQ10: snap:forPatient
#   sits outside GRAPH ?g; mda:impliesClinicalEvent is CONDITION -- entailed
#   per-tick onto a Stateful Process, exactly like hasRate/hasQualityState --
#   so it is matched inside GRAPH ?g, never in the accumulated background).
#   mda:triggeredByStructure (also CONDITION-scoped) is used only to fetch a
#   readable alarm label for each process, not to establish the finding
#   itself -- the core match is directly on impliesClinicalEvent, so the
#   generic-shared-Sensor/Signal collision CAT2a's own header documents
#   (walking alarm -> sensor -> signal -> metric across a device shared by
#   two archetypes) does not apply here: this query never walks that path.
#
# BUG FOUND AND FIXED (run against DATA/CQ_evaluation/events_data.csv via
# cq_temporal_QA.py, the same official pipeline CQ9/CQ10 use): the label
# OPTIONALs originally joined mda:triggeredByStructure directly onto
# ?cardiacProcess/?respiratoryProcess as if that property's target were the
# Metric. It isn't -- impliesClinicalEvent anchors on PhysiologicalProcess (see
# clinicalEvents.ttl's "RECONSIDERED AGAIN" note), two hops further out than
# where triggeredByStructure lands. Every label OPTIONAL therefore silently
# failed to bind on real, correct matches, and rdflib's GROUP_CONCAT(DISTINCT
# ...) raises NotBoundError rather than emitting an empty string when a whole
# group's aggregated variable is unbound -- so the query didn't just under-
# report, it crashed the run outright once cq11_pos (see below) supplied a
# genuine match. Fixed by extending the join one Metric->approximates->
# isPropertyOf hop further, onto the same Process the outer pattern already
# bound: `?cardiacAlarm mda:hasMessage/mda:triggeredByStructure/
# mda:approximates/mda:isPropertyOf ?cardiacProcess`.
#
# Validated end-to-end after the fix, via cq_temporal_QA.py against
# DATA/CQ_evaluation/events_data.csv's own cq11_pos/cq11_neg pair -- the same
# official pipeline and fixture CQ9/CQ10 are validated from, no longer via
# the DATA/CAT_evaluation workaround this note previously relied on:
# cq11_pos (PHILIPSMONITOR - Asystolie + PHILIPSMONITOR - Apneu, overlapping)
# fires exactly one row, correctly naming both alarms and
# clinicalEvent:CardioRespiratoryArrest; cq11_neg (SERVOU - Volume uit
# blokkade + PHILIPSMONITOR - Niet te leren ECG -- neither an Absent-rate
# HeartRate/RespirationRate archetype) and every other patient in the
# fixture (cq9_pos/neg, cq10_pos/neg) correctly produce zero rows.

PREFIX mda: <https://w3id.org/mda/ontology#>
PREFIX snap: <https://w3id.org/mda/snapshot/>
PREFIX clinicalEvent: <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/clinical-event/>

SELECT ?patient ?combinedEvent
       (GROUP_CONCAT(DISTINCT ?cardiacLabel; separator=" | ") AS ?cardiacAlarms)
       (GROUP_CONCAT(DISTINCT ?respiratoryLabel; separator=" | ") AS ?respiratoryAlarms) WHERE {
  ?g snap:forPatient ?patient .
  GRAPH ?g {
    ?cardiacProcess mda:impliesClinicalEvent clinicalEvent:CardiacArrest .
    ?respiratoryProcess mda:impliesClinicalEvent clinicalEvent:RespiratoryArrest .
    FILTER(?cardiacProcess != ?respiratoryProcess)
    OPTIONAL {
      ?cardiacAlarm mda:hasMessage/mda:triggeredByStructure/mda:approximates/mda:isPropertyOf ?cardiacProcess ;
                     mda:hasLabel ?cardiacLabel .
    }
    OPTIONAL {
      ?respiratoryAlarm mda:hasMessage/mda:triggeredByStructure/mda:approximates/mda:isPropertyOf ?respiratoryProcess ;
                         mda:hasLabel ?respiratoryLabel .
    }
  }
  BIND(clinicalEvent:CardioRespiratoryArrest AS ?combinedEvent)
}
GROUP BY ?patient ?combinedEvent
ORDER BY ?patient
